course: dictionary
lesson: 10102
title: One small word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Thing» is a small word that can mean many things. It is a noun, and the words around it show which meaning it has.
explain: Most often, a thing is an object you can name, like a ball or a chair. But «Pack your things» means your belongings, and «A strange thing happened» means an event.
explain: To find the meaning, read the whole sentence. Then try a clearer word such as "object", "belongings" or "event" in its place. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: A thing is any object you can name.
fact: «Things» can mean your belongings, as in «Pack your things».
fact: «A strange thing happened» uses thing to mean an event.
fact: Phrases such as «the same thing», «first thing» and «a thing or two» each have their own meaning, so check the whole phrase.
fact: In science, «living things» and «non-living things» are two groups of objects.
exercise: «Pack your things before we leave.» What does things mean here? | A strange event | A kind of weather | *Your belongings | An idea about the future
exercise: «A strange thing happened in the park.» What does thing mean? | A bench to sit on | A pet dog | A map of the park | *An event that happened
exercise: In science, the teacher sorts «living things» and «non-living things». What does things mean here? | Ideas about the future | Events in history | Belongings in a bag | *Objects, grouped by whether they are alive
test: «In a fair test you change only one thing.» What does thing mean here? | A type of plant | A strange event | *One single factor you can change | Your belongings
test: «If someone tells you a hurtful thing another person said, check with that person.» What does thing mean here? | *Words someone said | A park bench | A map of the town | A broken toy
exam: «Both things can be true: radiation hurts animals, yet people being gone helps them.» In this sentence, thing means: | A chair | A sports ball | A pet | *An idea or fact
